    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d877">

                <pb facs="1297" n="1283" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg1283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">895.50 Recovery/8–1948</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Director of the Budget</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pace</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lovett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-08-19">August 19,
                        1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Lovett</hi>: In accordance with our
                    agreement today, I am enclosing<anchor n="1" xml:id="d877-f1"/> for your comment
                    a proposed memorandum from the President to the effect that economic assistance
                    to Korea shall be undertaken by the Economic Cooperation Administration on
                    January 1, 1949 or in no event later than March 15, 1949. Enclosed likewise for
                    your comment is a proposed press statement of the President.</p>
                <p>Because of the top secret nature of the timing for the transfer and the
                    inadvisability of actual transfer at this time, it seems to me on further
                    reflection that a classified Presidential memorandum and a simple public
                    announcement will accomplish all the purposes you have in mind at this time, and
                    that the memorandum can be followed at a later date by the formal Executive
                    order.</p>
                <pb facs="1298" n="1284" xml:id="pg1284"/>
                <p>I congratulate each of you on the fine spirit of cooperation which made possible
                    our prompt agreement this morning.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank Pace, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d877-f1" n="1" xml:id="d877-f1-content">
                <p>Enclosures not attached to file copy. Marginal notations indicated that changes
                    suggested by the Department were accepted by Mr. Pace on August 20.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
